  "interpretation": [
    "Layer 63 shows a placement association after the specified adjustment. Reversing other options also changes average attention on a fixed slot, so the control does not isolate a causal effect of position.",
    "Neither layer's primary confirmation log-mass interval excludes zero. The pooled layer 63 association is suggestive. The archived next-choice logit crossover is more consistently positive across the pooled families.",
    "Family-cluster bootstrap intervals and exact sign flips use six families in confirmation and twelve pooled. Rotations are repeated presentations. The sign-flip calculation assumes exchangeable signs across family means and no cross-test correction was applied.",
    "The diagnostic does not estimate post-answer attention, final projected attention contribution to a choice logit, or the effect of a weight edit.",
    "The hashes bind the frozen inputs and local analysis artifacts. The raw prompts, token ledgers, activations and per-presentation measurements are not included with this aggregate evidence."
  ]
}
